#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "An overview of the available execution modes in Qiskit Runtime, including sessions, batch, and single jobs."
msgid "An overview of the available execution modes in Quantum Compute, including sessions, batch, and single jobs."
msgstr "Gambaran keseluruhan mod pelaksanaan yang tersedia dalam Qiskit Runtime, termasuk session, batch, dan job tunggal."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Introduction to Qiskit Runtime execution modes"
msgid "Introduction to IBM Quantum Compute Service execution modes"
msgstr "Pengenalan kepada mod pelaksanaan Qiskit Runtime"

#. type: Title #
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Introduction to Qiskit Runtime execution modes {#introduction-to-qiskit-runtime-execution-modes}"
msgid "Introduction to Quantum Compute execution modes {#introduction-to-quantum-compute-execution-modes}"
msgstr "Pengenalan kepada mod pelaksanaan Qiskit Runtime {#introduction-to-qiskit-runtime-execution-modes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "When Qiskit Runtime was introduced, users could only execute circuits as individual jobs. As different types of quantum workloads emerged, the need for different scheduling strategies became evident. The execution modes determine how your jobs are scheduled, and choosing the right execution mode allows your workload to run efficiently within your budget. There are three execution modes: job, session, and batch.\n"
msgid "When IBM Quantum Compute Service was introduced, users could only execute circuits as individual jobs. As different types of quantum workloads emerged, the need for different scheduling strategies became evident. The execution modes determine how your jobs are scheduled, and choosing the right execution mode allows your workload to run efficiently within your budget. There are three execution modes: job, session, and batch.\n"
msgstr "Apabila Qiskit Runtime diperkenalkan, pengguna hanya boleh melaksanakan litar sebagai job individu. Seiring dengan kemunculan pelbagai jenis beban kerja kuantum, keperluan untuk strategi penjadualan yang berbeza menjadi jelas. Mod pelaksanaan menentukan cara job anda dijadualkan, dan memilih mod pelaksanaan yang tepat membolehkan beban kerja anda berjalan dengan cekap dalam bajet anda. Terdapat tiga mod pelaksanaan: job, session, dan batch.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job mode {#job-mode}"
msgstr "Mod job {#job-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single primitive request made without a context manager. Circuits and inputs are packaged as primitive unified blocs (PUBs) and submitted as an execution task on the quantum computer. To run in job mode, specify `mode=backend` when instantiating a primitive. See [Estimator examples](/guides/estimator-examples) and [Sampler examples](/guides/sampler-examples) for usage.\n"
msgstr "Satu permintaan primitif tunggal yang dibuat tanpa pengurus konteks. Litar dan input dibungkus sebagai blok bersatu primitif (PUB) dan dihantar sebagai tugas pelaksanaan pada komputer kuantum. Untuk menjalankan dalam mod job, tentukan `mode=backend` semasa membuat instantiat sebuah primitif. Lihat [Contoh Estimator](/guides/estimator-examples) dan [Contoh Sampler](/guides/sampler-examples) untuk penggunaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"batch-mode\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"batch-mode\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch mode {#batch-mode}"
msgstr "Mod batch {#batch-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A multi-job manager for efficiently running experiments comprising multi-job workloads. These workloads are made up of independently executable jobs that have no conditional relationship with each other. With batch mode, users submit their jobs all at once. \n"
msgstr "Pengurus berbilang job untuk menjalankan eksperimen yang terdiri daripada beban kerja berbilang job dengan cekap. Beban kerja ini terdiri daripada job yang boleh dilaksanakan secara bebas dan tidak mempunyai hubungan bersyarat antara satu sama lain. Dengan mod batch, pengguna menghantar semua job mereka sekaligus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The system parallelizes or threads the pre-processing (classical computing) step of each primitive job to more tightly package quantum execution across jobs, and then runs the quantum execution of each job in quick succession to deliver the most efficient results. For further details about threading, see the [Execution mode FAQ page](/guides/execution-modes-faq#parallel).\n"
msgstr "Sistem ini memparalelkan atau menguruskan benang langkah pra-pemprosesan (pengkomputeran klasik) setiap job primitif untuk membungkus pelaksanaan kuantum merentas job dengan lebih padat, kemudian menjalankan pelaksanaan kuantum setiap job secara berturutan pantas untuk menghasilkan keputusan yang paling cekap. Untuk butiran lanjut tentang pengurusan benang, lihat [halaman FAQ mod pelaksanaan](/guides/execution-modes-faq#parallel).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A sets of jobs being run in batch mode.  The classical computation part of each job happens simultaneously, then all jobs are sent to the QPU.  The QPU is locked for your use from the time the first job reaches the QPU until the last job is done processing on the QPU.  There is no gap between jobs where the QPU is idle.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/batch.svg 'How a batch works')\n"
msgstr "![Satu set job yang dijalankan dalam mod batch. Bahagian pengkomputeran klasik setiap job berlaku serentak, kemudian semua job dihantar ke QPU. QPU dikunci untuk kegunaan anda dari masa job pertama tiba di QPU sehingga job terakhir selesai diproses pada QPU. Tiada jurang antara job di mana QPU melahu.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/batch.svg 'Cara batch berfungsi')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"- When batching, jobs are not guaranteed to run in the order they are submitted. Also, while your batch jobs will run as closely together as possible, they don't get exclusive access to the backend. Therefore, your batch jobs might run in parallel with other users' jobs if there is enough processing capacity on the QPU. Additionally, QPU calibration jobs could run between the batched jobs.\n"
"- The queuing time does not decrease for the first job submitted within a batch. Therefore, batches do not provide any benefits when running a single job.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Nota\">\n"
"- Semasa membuat batch, job tidak dijamin untuk berjalan mengikut urutan penghantarannya. Juga, walaupun job batch anda akan berjalan sedekat mungkin antara satu sama lain, mereka tidak mendapat akses eksklusif kepada Backend. Oleh itu, job batch anda mungkin berjalan selari dengan job pengguna lain jika terdapat kapasiti pemprosesan yang mencukupi pada QPU. Selain itu, job penentukuran QPU boleh berjalan di antara job batch.\n"
"- Masa baris gilir tidak berkurang untuk job pertama yang dihantar dalam batch. Oleh itu, batch tidak memberikan sebarang faedah ketika menjalankan satu job sahaja.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run in batch mode, specify `mode=batch` when instantiating a primitive or run the job in a batch context manager. See [Run jobs in a batch](/guides/run-jobs-batch) for examples.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan dalam mod batch, tentukan `mode=batch` semasa membuat instantiat sebuah primitif atau jalankan job dalam pengurus konteks batch. Lihat [Jalankan job dalam batch](/guides/run-jobs-batch) untuk contoh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"session-mode\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"session-mode\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session mode {#session-mode}"
msgstr "Mod session {#session-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dedicated window for running a multi-job workload.  During this window, the user has exclusive access of the system and no other jobs can run - including calibration jobs. This allows users to experiment with variational algorithms in a more predictable way and even run multiple experiments simultaneously, taking advantage of parallelism in the stack. Using sessions helps avoid delays caused by queuing each job separately, which can be particularly useful for iterative tasks that require frequent communication between classical and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr "Tetingkap khusus untuk menjalankan beban kerja berbilang job. Semasa tetingkap ini, pengguna mempunyai akses eksklusif kepada sistem dan tiada job lain boleh berjalan — termasuk job penentukuran. Ini membolehkan pengguna bereksperimen dengan algoritma variasi dengan cara yang lebih boleh diramalkan dan malah menjalankan pelbagai eksperimen serentak, memanfaatkan keselarian dalam tindanan. Menggunakan session membantu mengelakkan kelewatan akibat baris gilir setiap job secara berasingan, yang amat berguna untuk tugas berulang yang memerlukan komunikasi kerap antara sumber klasik dan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A sets of jobs being run in session mode and the other is being run in batch mode.  Between each job is the interactive TTL (interactive time to live).  The active window starts when the first job starts and ends after the last job is completed. After the final job of the first set of jobs completes, the active window ends and the session is paused (but not closed).  Another set of jobs then starts and jobs continue in a similar manner. The QPU is reserved for your use during the entire session.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/session.svg 'How a session works')\n"
msgstr "![Satu set job yang dijalankan dalam mod session dan satu lagi dijalankan dalam mod batch. Antara setiap job ialah TTL interaktif (masa hidup interaktif). Tetingkap aktif bermula apabila job pertama bermula dan berakhir selepas job terakhir selesai. Selepas job terakhir set job pertama selesai, tetingkap aktif berakhir dan session dijeda (tetapi tidak ditutup). Set job lain kemudian bermula dan job diteruskan dengan cara yang serupa. QPU dikhaskan untuk kegunaan anda sepanjang tempoh session.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/session.svg 'Cara session berfungsi')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run in session mode, specify `mode=session` when instantiating a primitive, or run the job in a session context manager. See [Run jobs in a session](/guides/run-jobs-session) for examples.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan dalam mod session, tentukan `mode=session` semasa membuat instantiat sebuah primitif, atau jalankan job dalam pengurus konteks session. Lihat [Jalankan job dalam session](/guides/run-jobs-session) untuk contoh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"- The queuing time does not decrease for the first job submitted within a session. Therefore, sessions do not provide any benefits when running a single job.\n"
"- Open Plan users cannot submit session jobs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Nota\">\n"
"- Masa baris gilir tidak berkurang untuk job pertama yang dihantar dalam session. Oleh itu, session tidak memberikan sebarang faedah ketika menjalankan satu job sahaja.\n"
"- Pengguna Open Plan tidak boleh menghantar job session.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Basic workflow {#basic-workflow}"
msgstr "Aliran kerja asas {#basic-workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basic workflow for batches and sessions is similar:\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja asas untuk batch dan session adalah serupa:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first job in a batch or session enters the normal queue. For batches, the entire batch of jobs is scheduled together.\n"
msgstr "Job pertama dalam batch atau session memasuki baris gilir biasa. Untuk batch, keseluruhan set job batch dijadualkan bersama.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the first job starts running, the maximum time to live (TTL) timer starts, and does not stop or pause until the end is reached.\n"
msgstr "Apabila job pertama mula berjalan, pemasa masa hidup maksimum (TTL) bermula, dan tidak berhenti atau dijeda sehingga tamat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The interactive TTL timer starts after each job is completed.  If there are no workload jobs ready within the interactive TTL window, the workload is temporarily deactivated and normal job selection resumes. A job can reactivate the deactivated workload if the batch or session has not reached its maximum TTL value.\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The job must go through the normal queue to reactivate the workload.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Pemasa TTL interaktif bermula selepas setiap job selesai. Jika tiada job beban kerja yang sedia dalam tetingkap TTL interaktif, beban kerja dinyahaktifkan sementara dan pemilihan job biasa disambung semula. Sebuah job boleh mengaktifkan semula beban kerja yang dinyahaktifkan jika batch atau session belum mencapai nilai TTL maksimumnya.\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Job tersebut perlu melalui baris gilir biasa untuk mengaktifkan semula beban kerja.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the maximum TTL value is reached, the workload ends and any remaining queued jobs fail. Any job currently running won't run to completion if doing so would exceed the instance's cost limit.\n"
msgstr "Jika nilai TTL maksimum dicapai, beban kerja berakhir dan sebarang job yang masih dalam baris gilir akan gagal. Mana-mana job yang sedang berjalan tidak akan diselesaikan jika berbuat demikian akan melebihi had kos instans.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following video illustrates the basic workflow, using sessions as an example:\n"
msgstr "Video berikut menggambarkan aliran kerja asas, menggunakan session sebagai contoh:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"134371940\" title=\"A user starts a session job and becomes the priority user.  They submit jobs to the QPU while other users wait. After the prioritized user's session finishes, the next person's jobs can begin processing.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"134371940\" title=\"Seorang pengguna memulakan job session dan menjadi pengguna keutamaan. Mereka menghantar job ke QPU sementara pengguna lain menunggu. Selepas session pengguna yang diutamakan selesai, job orang seterusnya boleh mula diproses.\"/>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For full details about the TTL timers, see the [Maximum execution time](/guides/max-execution-time) guide.\n"
msgstr "Untuk butiran penuh tentang pemasa TTL, lihat panduan [Masa pelaksanaan maksimum](/guides/max-execution-time).\n"

